import debug.dl

to get [the clicked Studio debug row of] {C string:label} [in] {a pointer to UI view:view}:
    set node to the control labeled label in (view's instance)
    set position to -1
    if (view's input kind = 2) and (view's input code = 1):
        set point to the UI cursor in view
        set run to the UI text hit at point in view
        if run != (0 as a pointer to UI text run):
            if run's source's element = node:
                set position to run's start
    else if (view's key press = 257) and (view's text focus = node):
        set position to view's selection's caret
    if position < 0:
        return -1
    set text to (the UI value for node in (view's instance))'s text
    set row to 0
    loop index from 0 to position:
        if (the character at index in text) = (10 as a byte):
            increment row
    return row

to get [read Studio debugger] {a pointer:context} [in] {a pointer to UI view:view}:
    set state to context as a pointer to website state
    set session to the address of (state's studio debug)
    if (state's route != "/ide/index.html") or (session's paused = false):
        return false
    set row to the clicked Studio debug row of "Debug stack" in view
    if row >= 0:
        if row < session's snapshot's length:
            clear Studio debug marks in state
            set session's selected frame to row
            display the Studio debug frame in state
            show Studio debug location (the JSON value at index row in (session's snapshot)) in state
        return true
    set row to the clicked Studio debug row of "Debug variables" in view
    if row >= 0:
        if (row < session's rows' length) and (session's query = 0):
            set item to the JSON value at index row in (session's rows)
            set reference to (the JSON number named "reference" in item) as an integer
            set start to (the JSON number named "start" in item) as an integer
            if reference > 0:
                set key to formatted "{reference}"
                if (start = 0) and (session's expanded has JSON member named key):
                    remove JSON member key from (session's expanded)
                else if (start > 0) or ((session's children has JSON member named key) = false):
                    request Studio debug variables reference starting at start in state
                else:
                    set JSON member (JSON flag key is true) in (session's expanded)
                display the Studio debug frame in state
        return true
    return false

to [initialize Studio debugging in] {a pointer to website state:state}:
    set session to the address of (state's studio debug)
    set session's snapshot to a new JSON value of kind the JSON array kind
    set session's rows to a new JSON value of kind the JSON array kind
    set session's breakpoints to a new JSON value of kind the JSON array kind
    set session's children to a new JSON value of kind the JSON object kind
    set session's expanded to a new JSON value of kind the JSON object kind
    set session's overlay to a UI overlay in (state's view) with context (state as a pointer) handling input ((the function named "read Studio debugger $ in $") as a pointer) painting (0 as a pointer) closing (0 as a pointer)
    display Studio debug controls in state

to [close Studio debugging in] {a pointer to website state:state}:
    set session to the address of (state's studio debug)
    detach UI overlay (session's overlay) in (state's view)
    set state's language's tools' runtime values to 0 as a pointer to JSON value
    free session's snapshot
    free session's rows
    free session's breakpoints
    free session's children
    free session's expanded
